 ## Overview
-A fragment shader that rasterizes geometry into a 3D grid volume by mapping clip-space coordinates to grid indices and writing a value to a structured buffer [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Rasterization-based Voxelization](908-rasterization-based-voxelization.md) by operating directly on the GPU via fragment shaders to produce volumetric data (binary occupancy or spherical harmonic coefficients) rather than 2D buffers, and from [Mesh-to-Voxel Geometry Shader](2800-mesh-to-voxel-geometry-shader.md) by relying on standard rasterization pipelines rather than explicit geometry shader topology expansion [S1, S2, unofficial].
